  "enhanced_information": "Cilostazol inhibits phosphodiesterase 3, leading to increased cAMP levels in vascular smooth muscle, resulting in vasodilation and decreased systemic vascular resistance. This mechanism can lead to a compensatory increase in cardiac output due to reduced afterload, which may result in an increase in left ventricular end-diastolic volume. However, the effect on chronotropy is less clear, as vasodilation may lead to a compensatory increase in heart rate, but this does not directly imply a negative chronotropic effect. Therefore, the most supported expected effect of cilostazol, based on its mechanism of action, is an increase in left ventricular end-diastolic volume.",
